{
  "name": "418. Gemini Omni video on the Interactions API: create, query, cancel and keyed download (gemini omni video, provider error fixture)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-6538 (contract C4, C5, C7, C9) on the unified video routes for the gemini provider. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The gemini provider of that config has the fixture as its base URL, and the fixture serves the Interactions API: POST /interactions answers a running interaction, GET /interactions/{id} one whose state its id names (omni-running, omni-completed, omni-incomplete), POST /interactions/{id}/cancel a cancelled one, and GET /files/omni-file:download the video bytes. Before the change an Omni model was sent to models/{model}:predictLongRunning, which the fixture has no answer for, the cancel route answered provider_cancel_unsupported for every id, and an interaction id was not a valid task id. Row 1 creates a task and reads the body the fixture received: background true, seconds as duration, aspect_ratio, resolution, delivery uri, callback_url in webhook_config.uris and client_reference_id in webhook_config.user_metadata. Rows 2 and 3: a field the Interactions API has no field for (size) and a control field no Gemini API takes (expires_after_seconds) are refused with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter. Row 4: the query of a completed interaction is completed with provider_status, one videos entry of type content with no url, usage.output_tokens from the video modality and expires_at 48 hours after completed_at. Row 5: a status with no task-object status of the same meaning (incomplete) stays in provider_status and reports in_progress. Row 6: cancel of a running interaction calls the vendor cancel and returns cancelled. Row 7: cancel of a completed interaction is 400 provider_cancel_unsupported; it also reads the fixture: the only cancel that arrived is the running interaction's, so the refused cancel and the refused creates made no upstream write. Row 8: /content returns the Gemini Files artifact fetched with the key. The vertex provider's host is computed from the key's location and cannot be pointed at the fixture, so the same behaviour on vertex is pinned by the Go tests (core/providers/vertex/interactions_test.go).",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "418.1 gemini/gemini-omni-1.1-flash POST /v1/videos creates a background interaction with the unified fields in the Interactions body (gemini omni video)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"gemini/gemini-omni-1.1-flash\",\n  \"prompt\": \"a marble on a track\",\n  \"seconds\": \"8\",\n  \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\",\n  \"resolution\": \"720p\",\n  \"callback_url\": \"https://hooks.example.test/v/task_418\",\n  \"client_reference_id\": \"task_418\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/videos",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "videos"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var FX = pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') || 'http://127.0.0.1:8791';",
              "pm.test('the create returns a running task whose id names the interaction kind', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.id, 'id: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('interactions%2Fomni-running:gemini');",
              "  pm.expect(j.status, 'status: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('in_progress');",
              "  pm.expect(j.provider_status, 'provider_status: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('in_progress');",
              "});",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: FX + '/__wire', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture received the Interactions body', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    var calls = res.json().data[0].calls.filter(function (c) { return c.path === '/pp/gemini/interactions' && c.body.indexOf('task_418') !== -1; });",
              "    pm.expect(calls.length, 'no create reached /pp/gemini/interactions: ' + res.text()).to.be.above(0);",
              "    var b = JSON.parse(calls[calls.length - 1].body);",
              "    pm.expect(b.model, calls[calls.length - 1].body).to.eql('gemini-omni-1.1-flash');",
              "    pm.expect(b.background, 'background').to.eql(true);",
              "    pm.expect(b.input, 'input').to.eql([{ type: 'text', text: 'a marble on a track' }]);",
              "    pm.expect(b.response_format, 'response_format').to.eql({ type: 'video', delivery: 'uri', aspect_ratio: '16:9', duration: '8s', resolution: '720p' });",
              "    pm.expect(b.webhook_config, 'webhook_config').to.eql({ uris: ['https://hooks.example.test/v/task_418'], user_metadata: { client_reference_id: 'task_418' } });",
              "    pm.expect(b.seconds, 'the unified name must not be sent').to.eql(undefined);",
              "    pm.expect(b.callback_url, 'the unified name must not be sent').to.eql(undefined);",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
